# v30 OVERLAY (2026-10-31, my call under the reward delegation): a PARTIAL
# charge for driving away from the goal -- 0.3 of what approaching pays.
#
# WHY. The paired wrong-goal eval on Town02, n=100, priced both ends of this
# dial and they fail in opposite ways:
#
#   v27, retreat charged in full:  true 0.470  wrong 0.300  gap +0.170 (p=0.0033)
#        The policy USES the goal image -- and the run collapsed, because the
#        charge drove the goal value to -20..-48 and a -1 crossing became the
#        cheap way out.
#   v29, retreat free:             true 0.480  wrong 0.470  gap +0.010 (p=1.00)
#        Stable to 1M, no collapse, and the policy IGNORES the goal image: it
#        drives the lane and collects whatever goal falls inside the 2 m
#        arrival radius. Its 0.480 is lane following, not navigation.
#
# Charging for retreat is what forces a CHOICE OF DIRECTION, and the image is
# the only thing that says which direction; free retreat removed the collapse
# and the reason to look at the image together. 0.3 is chosen so a wrong turn
# still costs -- about a third of a metre's pay per metre -- while the worst
# sustained value a lost car can reach is roughly a third of v27's, which is
# where the cheap-exit arithmetic tipped over.
#
# JUDGE THIS RUN ON THE PAIRED GAP, NOT THE SUCCESS RATE. A run that scores
# 0.48 by lane following is worse than one scoring 0.47 that navigates; v29
# proved the two are indistinguishable without the wrong-goal arm.
. "$REPO/slurm/v29_overlay.env"
unset ROUTE_PROGRESS_POSITIVE
export ROUTE_RETREAT_SCALE=0.3
